= Underfitting — Simple =

'''Underfitting''' happens when a machine-learning model has not learned enough of the useful structure in the task.

It may perform badly on both the training data and new data.

This can happen because the model is too restricted, is trained poorly, uses weak features, or is regularized too strongly.

Underfitting is not simply “the model is small.”

